# Phase Three — Tiferes: Tree Resource Realism Final Plan

The Awtsmoos renews soil and crown, thirst and light; Awtsmoos.com joins resource and development in one pre-skeleton covenant so every later LOD beholds the same tree in sight.

## Exact code wave
1. NEW `src/core/tzomayach/TreeResourceDevelopment.js`
   - pure immutable resource intent;
   - reads explicit environment/development resource fields only;
   - derives moisture, fertility, heatStress, soilDepth, shade, resourceSupport, waterStress, rootInvestment, canopyAllocation, foliageSupport, heightSupport;
   - no RNG and no renderer state.
2. REWRITE `TreeDevelopmentProfile.js`
   - preserve succession/age/vigor/competition/light/wind fields;
   - attach resource intent additively;
   - derive structural scalars by composing succession with resources;
   - preserve exact old behavior when no resource intent exists.
3. REWRITE `TreeDevelopmentForcing.js`
   - split vector math into documented helpers;
   - use resource stress only through bounded angle/gnarliness/force coefficients;
   - preserve existing default behavior when resources are neutral.
4. REWRITE `TreeDevelopmentConfig.js`
   - remain the only pre-skeleton mutation boundary;
   - apply resource-aware height/crown/trunk/branch/foliage scales through existing branch/leaves keys;
   - no quality/LOD inputs.
5. Do not change `TreeLivingManifest`, `TreeHydraulicState`, or LOD generation unless tests prove a compatibility gap.

## Verification after code-first completion
- full readback of all touched source;
- syntax, tabs, <=120-line source gate;
- existing `treeAnatomyAuthority.test.mjs`;
- existing `treeBiologyOutputCompatibility.test.mjs`;
- existing `treeLivingManifest.test.mjs`;
- NEW `treeEnvironmentalDevelopment.test.mjs` proving:
  - no-environment behavior remains deterministic;
  - explicit drought and fertile/moist environments create deterministic but distinct skeletons;
  - post-skeleton living hydraulic tuning still preserves skeleton identity;
  - every geometry/LOD/anatomy/living hash binds to the resource-shaped skeleton;
  - resource signals remain bounded/immutable.

## NEXT_ACTION
Re-read TreeDevelopmentProfile, TreeDevelopmentForcing, and TreeDevelopmentConfig, then write the complete code wave before testing.
